  "final_message": "I put `channel` back, so the `analytics-ingest` check (ARCH-4) should pass again. I only ran the typecheck, which passes. I haven't run the tests or `npm run arch`. I couldn't run ARCH-4 itself, because it isn't defined in this repo.\n\nMy earlier \"nothing reads it\" was wrong. `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as an enum of `web`, `store` or `marketplace`. Removing the field broke that contract.\n\nI undid the whole removal by hand, because `git checkout` was denied. The source, tests and docs are back to their original state. `OrderPlaced` again carries `channel`, and the order model, `POST /orders` parsing and validation are as before.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. After that, removing it from the event would likely mean a new `schemaVersion`. Tell me if you want me to redo the removal once that team has changed their side.",
